    <!-- ============ Push-and-turn safety cap (Tasks 232-233) ============
         The cap rides on a vertical slide (k_c = 2000 N/m) and spins freely on its own hinge. Its six teeth sit 10 mm
         above the twelve teeth of the ratchet ring, so the ring (the closure state) turns only while the cap is pressed
         down by more than 10 mm, i.e. F_z = k_c dz > 20 N; below that the cap freewheels. A spring-loaded plunger with two
         balls straddles a bump on the ring rim at 0 deg (the closed detent). Ring hold: joint dry friction plus the detent.
         A fixed lip on the bottle covers the ring, so the ring cannot be turned except through the cap teeth; a
